{"id":"sponsored-dollars-to-connected","title":"Sponsored dollars going to connected beneficiaries, against the Board","question":"Do an official’s own donors and requested-payment partners show up more in the files that official sponsors than in everybody else’s files?","finding":"Across all sponsors, 7.0% of sponsored money files (7.4% of the dollars in their titles) name a beneficiary with a money link to the sponsor; the same officials’ money-linked organizations appear in 4.5% of the files they did not sponsor while in office (more than chance would produce). 3 officials of 29 show a higher share in their own files than in others’ by more than chance (Mark Farrell, David Campos, Myrna Melgar), and 0 a lower one; for the rest the difference is within chance or too small to test.","how":"For every official with at least five passed, sponsored contracts, grant agreements, leases or loans naming an outside organization: the share of those files (and of the dollars in their titles) whose beneficiary has a money link to the official (the links of the previous screen, lobbying left out). The comparison is the share of files introduced while the official was in office, sponsored by somebody else, that name one of the same official’s money-linked organizations. The two shares are compared with Fisher’s exact test on file counts; “more than chance” means a probability under 5%. “Any link” adds lobbyists’ reported contacts. The last row pools every sponsor.","limits":"Being connected is not being corrupt. A higher share in one’s own files can also follow from how files are sponsored: a supervisor sponsors files for organizations in the district, whose staff are also the district’s donors; the Mayor sponsors more money files than any supervisor and a Mayor’s donor list is long, so the Mayor’s own-file share is high by construction. Dollar shares are driven by a handful of very large contracts, so the test uses file counts. Links are counted at any date, before or after the file. Amounts, parties and dates taken from Board file titles are read by machine: in a hand check of 50 titles, 11 had at least one field read wrongly (4 after later fixes).","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"official","t":"Official","type":"person"},{"k":"files","t":"Sponsored money files with an outside beneficiary","type":"int"},{"k":"dollars","t":"Dollars in titles","type":"usd"},{"k":"connectedFiles","t":"Naming a money-linked beneficiary","type":"int"},{"k":"connectedDollars","t":"Dollars to money-linked beneficiaries","type":"usd"},{"k":"shareFiles","t":"Share of own files","type":"pct"},{"k":"shareDollars","t":"Share of own dollars","type":"pct"},{"k":"otherShare","t":"Same organizations in others’ files","type":"pct"},{"k":"otherFiles","t":"Others’ files while in office","type":"int"},{"k":"chance","t":"Difference","type":"text"},{"k":"anyLinkShare","t":"Share with any link, lobbying included","type":"pct"}],"rows":[{"official":"All sponsors together (the Board as a whole)","files":915,"dollars":30796941909,"connectedFiles":64,"connectedDollars":2272760394,"shareFiles":0.0699,"shareDollars":0.0738,"anyLinkShare":0.1005,"otherFiles":5796,"otherShare":0.0449,"otherShareDollars":null,"chance":"more than chance would produce"},{"official":"Mark Farrell","files":15,"dollars":203801055,"connectedFiles":4,"connectedDollars":132429557,"shareFiles":0.2667,"shareDollars":0.6498,"anyLinkShare":0.3333,"otherFiles":110,"otherShare":0.0091,"otherShareDollars":0.0,"chance":"more than chance would produce"},{"official":"David Campos","files":8,"dollars":202781274,"connectedFiles":2,"connectedDollars":1,"shareFiles":0.25,"shareDollars":0.0,"anyLinkShare":0.25,"otherFiles":56,"otherShare":0.0179,"otherShareDollars":0.0714,"chance":"more than chance would produce"},{"official":"Myrna Melgar","files":27,"dollars":1218071999,"connectedFiles":5,"connectedDollars":532049155,"shareFiles":0.1852,"shareDollars":0.4368,"anyLinkShare":0.1852,"otherFiles":355,"otherShare":0.0535,"oth